---
const guide = '/images/webmaker-guide';
---
<div class="tutorial-intro"><p>WebMAKER 0.1.1 brings the guide, diagrams, sample site, and Studio interface into English. Clone the starter, customize a club site and publish it with GitHub Pages. Download Studio to edit locally and prepare Git publishing. The diagrams illustrate the workflow.</p><p><a class="inline-link" href="https://github.com/PlayMAKER-apps/webmaker" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WebMAKER repository ↗</a> · <a class="inline-link" href="https://github.com/PlayMAKER-apps/webmaker/releases/tag/v0.1.1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Studio release ↗</a></p></div>
<nav class="tutorial-paths" aria-label="Choose a tutorial path"><a href="#user-guide">For users: install & use</a><a href="#developer-guide">For contributors & developers</a></nav>
<div class="tutorial-path-heading" id="user-guide"><p class="eyebrow">For users</p><h3>Create & publish your club site</h3><p>The starter includes three themes, synthetic data and a GitHub Pages workflow. Studio 0.1.1 is available for Windows.</p></div>
<ol class="tutorial-steps">
  <li class="tutorial-step"><div class="step-copy"><span class="section-kicker">01 / Start</span><h3>Clone and create an instance</h3><p>Install Node.js 22+ and Git, clone WebMAKER and run the initializer. The new club folder has its own data and Pages workflow, without Nerone history or media.</p><pre><code>git clone https://github.com/PlayMAKER-apps/webmaker.git
cd webmaker
node scripts/init-club.mjs ../my-club</code></pre></div><figure><img src={`${guide}/01-themes.svg`} alt="Illustration comparing Bold, Classic and Dynamic layouts with the same Aurora club data" width="960" height="440" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>One club, three site layouts. Illustration.</figcaption></figure></li>
  <li class="tutorial-step"><div class="step-copy"><span class="section-kicker">02 / Customize</span><h3>Add your identity and content</h3><p>Edit <code>site/data/club.yaml</code> for club name, URL, repository, logo, colors, sport and <code>theme</code>. Replace demo teams, players, games and news in <code>site/data/</code> and <code>site/content/news/</code>. Keep IDs stable after publishing. Only add images you may use.</p><p>For AI help, give an agent the config and synthetic examples, ask it to edit content or theme settings, review the diff and run the build. Keep private player data and credentials out of prompts.</p></div><figure><img src={`${guide}/02-studio.svg`} alt="Illustration of WebMAKER Studio club and theme editor, local save, validation and publishing" width="960" height="440" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Studio separates local save, push and completed deployment. Illustration.</figcaption></figure></li>
  <li class="tutorial-step"><div class="step-copy"><span class="section-kicker">03 / Preview & publish</span><h3>Use GitHub Pages</h3><p>From the club folder, run <code>cd site</code>, <code>npm ci</code>, <code>npm test</code> and <code>npm run build</code>. Create an empty GitHub repository for the club. In <code>club.yaml</code>, set <code>repository_url</code> to its GitHub URL, <code>site_url</code> to the Pages URL and <code>base_path</code> to the repository name with a leading slash. Initialize and push the club's <code>main</code> branch, then select <strong>Settings → Pages → GitHub Actions</strong>. Wait for Actions to finish and check the live site. The repository README has the exact Git commands.</p><pre><code>cd ../my-club/site
npm ci
npm test
npm run build</code></pre></div><figure><img src={`${guide}/03-pages.svg`} alt="Four illustrated steps: clone, customize, enable GitHub Pages Actions, verify the live site" width="960" height="440" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Publishing steps. Illustration.</figcaption></figure></li>
  <li class="tutorial-step"><div class="step-copy"><span class="section-kicker">04 / Studio</span><h3>Edit without a web admin</h3><p><a class="inline-link" href="https://github.com/PlayMAKER-apps/webmaker/releases/download/v0.1.1/WebMAKER.Studio_0.1.1_x64-setup.exe">Download WebMAKER Studio 0.1.1 for Windows ↗</a> and install Git for Windows with Git Credential Manager. The installer is unsigned. Open one club repository at a time, save locally, validate, inspect the publishing preview, push and check GitHub Actions. Studio does not store a personal access token.</p></div></li>
</ol>
<div class="tutorial-path-heading" id="developer-guide"><p class="eyebrow">For contributors & developers</p><h3>Improve the open source project</h3><p>WebMAKER is public under Apache-2.0 with a NOTICE attribution. Use the source, tests and shared format notes to propose focused changes.</p></div>
<div class="developer-guide-grid">
  <div class="developer-guide-card"><h4>1. Build and test locally</h4><p>The site uses Node.js 22+; Studio also needs Rust/MSVC, Visual Studio Build Tools and WebView2 on Windows. Use synthetic fixtures. A successful push does not prove Pages deployment.</p><pre><code>cd site &amp;&amp; npm ci &amp;&amp; npm test &amp;&amp; npm run build
cd ../studio &amp;&amp; npm ci &amp;&amp; npm test &amp;&amp; npm run build
cargo test --manifest-path src-tauri/Cargo.toml</code></pre></div>
  <div class="developer-guide-card"><h4>2. Propose a focused improvement</h4><p>Open an issue in <a class="inline-link" href="https://github.com/PlayMAKER-apps/webmaker/issues">WebMAKER</a>, fork the repository, create a branch and send a pull request with a clear user workflow and tests. Good early contributions include an editor driven by sport profiles, accessibility checks, visual regression tests and extraction of the social graphics engine after asset review.</p></div>
  <div class="developer-guide-card"><h4>3. Respect shared data</h4><p>TagMAKER imports <code>teams.yaml</code>, <code>players/*.yaml</code> and <code>rosters.csv</code> from a WebMAKER club. Its 0.1 JSON event timeline is a separate contract from WebMAKER's per-game statistics CSV. Preserve stable IDs and provide migrations for schema changes. See the <a class="inline-link" href="https://github.com/PlayMAKER-apps/playmaker-schema" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">PlayMAKER schema repository ↗</a>.</p></div>
</div>
